%U A399321 1,4,2,6,1,2,2,3,8,2,8,4,4,9,1,4,7,9,3,1,3,5,2,8,7,9,2,7,1,0,9,6,6,0,0,3,9
%N A399321 Decimal expansion of Pi*(1 + gamma)/32, where gamma is Euler's constant A001620.
%C A399321 A384541 = (1/32)*(2 - gamma)*Pi = (1/32)*(b + 1 - gamma)*Pi = lim_{epsilon -> 0} -(Pi/32)*(1/((-1 + epsilon)*epsilon) + zeta(1 + epsilon)) = lim_{k->oo} -Pi/32*(Sum_{n=b+1..k} 1/n - (1 + log(k))), where Sum_{n=b+1..k} 1/n^s = zeta(s) - b.
%C A399321 Equals A215722 - A019675, which conjecturally equals Integral(t=0..oo, (1-12*t^2)/(1+4*t^2)^3) * integral(s=1/2..oo, log |zeta(s + i*t)|) - Integral_{x=0..oo} 1 - Sum_{t>=0} (1 - 12*(t*x)^2)/(1 + 4*(t*x)^2)^3 dx. Those two integrals share the same kernel but with a different number of variables.
%F A399321 Equals lim_{epsilon -> 0} (Pi/32)*(1/((-1 + epsilon)*epsilon) - zeta'(1 + epsilon)/zeta(1 + epsilon)). This is analogous to replacing zeta(s) - b in the formula for A384541, with -zeta'(s)/zeta(s) since -zeta'(s)/zeta(s) = lim_{c->1} zeta(s)*zeta(c)/zeta(c+s-1) - z, where z = zeta(c) is analogous to b = 1 in the comment for A384541. z = zeta(c) is the first column in matrix A191898 and b = 1 is A191898(1, 1). Zeta(s) - b is the Dirichlet generating function for the first row of matrix A191898, with the first term b = 1 removed. -zeta'(s)/zeta(s) corresponds to matrix A191898, with the first column z = zeta(c) removed.
%e A399321 0.1548427858119186480648680598297044657282760...
%t A399321 RealDigits[N[-(1/32) (1 + EulerGamma) Pi, 105]][[1]]
%Y A399321 Cf. A215722, A019675, A384541, A191898, A336308.
%K A399321 nonn,cons,new
%O A399321 0,2
